IMPORT prelude

-- Long Service Leave Act 1976 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library, and defines no YMD. Dates are compared by serial.
--
-- "n months after" a day is read as the corresponding day of the month n months on, or the last day of that month if
-- it has no corresponding day (31 August + 6 months = 28 or 29 February). The Legislation Act 2001 (ACT), which says
-- how ACT periods are counted (ss 151-151C), is not deposited: this reading is fork F1 in NOTES.md.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Long Service Leave Act 1976`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day (before it, if n is negative).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

-- The number of days in a calendar month (the first of the next month, less the first of this month).
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The day that is n whole calendar months (n of 0 or more) after a day: the corresponding day of the month n months
-- on, or the last day of that month if it is shorter (fork F1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the first day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `months after` `the first day` MEANS
    IF `the day number` AT MOST `the length of month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the target month` `the target year`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the length of month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the day number` MEANS DATE_DAY `the first day`
        `the month count` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the first day` MINUS 1 PLUS n
        `the target month` MEANS (`the month count` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the first day` PLUS TRUNC (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12) 0

-- The number of whole calendar months from one day to a later day (0 if the later day is not later): the most n
-- for which the day n months after the first is on or before the second.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole months from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` MEANS
    IF `the rough count` LESS THAN 1
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the day` (`the day` `the rough count` `months after` `the first day`) `is on or before` `the last day`
         THEN `the rough count`
         ELSE `the rough count` MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `the rough count` MEANS
            ((DATE_YEAR `the last day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the first day`) TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the last day` MINUS DATE_MONTH `the first day`)
